A||||6||sid1200||88 suspension problems
Z||000000||sid1200||08-13-99||03:06 AM||||I just bought an 88GT with 23k miles, and am having the following problems<br>the suspension/shock/struts/etc squeak almost continuously on most any bump/irregularity.  the handling/shock absorbtion seems good,  what can I do to fix this.<p>also the car seem to pull a little to the right under braking, but not normally.<br>and what should I do maintenece wise. was thinking of repalcing the clutch/brake/coolant  <br>what else should I do.<p>
Z||000001||lowCG||08-13-99||05:00 AM||||The little rubber seals on top of the struts,where the piston rod goes in are probably dry,or were dry,and when it was driven,left rubber residue on the rod.<br>Just a guess.<br>If the car sat for a long time,the brakes may need a rebuild,new seals.
Z||000002||Cooter||08-13-99||06:52 AM||||Dont forget to replace the rubber brake hoses too. They get internal blockage that causes the car to pull under braking.
Z||000003||Dale||08-13-99||12:26 PM||||Try bleeding the brakes first.  Clutch etc. if its not bad why fix it.  Sometimes the springs can squeak as well check to see if the rubber on the back strut is still in place, and also see if the spring in front may be rubbing on the bumpstop tower inside the spring.  
Z||000004||Bruce||08-14-99||12:07 PM||||Does the 88 have lubrication fittings? I had to tell the mechanic several times before he believed me that my 86 needed to be lubed, per the owners' manual.<br>Anyway, if it does and hasn't been lubed for awhile, that could cause some squeaking.
Z||000005||lowCG||08-15-99||02:12 AM||||Factory ball joints are usually non-greasable,aftermarket ones more often come with a fitting,that's all there'd be to lube under the car.
Z||000006||mwbackus||08-15-99||02:44 AM||||The upper and lower ball joints, and the tie rod ends have lubrication fittings on my formula.  I dont know the history of the car so it could be alot of aftermarket front end parts.  But, given the condition of things like shocks (they were original with 107k) I highly doubt they replaced anything. :-(<p>Mike
